# bug-nilpy-every-lambda-is-interpreted-instead-of-compiled
#
# A lambda body with NO CALL in it was never lifted: PyLambdaBodyIsLiftable
# required `sawCall or nestedLambda`, so every call-free body fell to the pyeval
# SOURCE closure and was re-walked by the tree-walker on each call.
#
# That covered the most ordinary lambdas there are — `lambda r: r[1]` (the
# Python sort-key idiom), `lambda v: -v`, `lambda x: x * 2` — and it was not
# free. Measured over 200k calls through map():
#
#     lifted (compiled)      1.0 us/call
#     pyeval source closure  6.9 us/call    6.9x
#     CPython, either form   0.1 us/call    we lost to an INTERPRETER by 69x
#
# The old gate's justification was "a call-less body already works through the
# pyeval closure, and lifting it would be a behaviour change for no gain". The
# premise held; the conclusion did not.
#
# This file pins the shapes that route changed for. Every one of them was
# INTERPRETED before and is COMPILED now, so it is the lift — not the
# interpreter — that has to get them right. Answers diffed against CPython.
#
# Compiled-ness itself is not observable from program output (both routes
# produce the same answers, which is why this was invisible). The direct oracle
# is the body source text no longer being embedded in the binary:
#     strings <bin> | grep -c 'return '     11 before, 0 after

xs = [5, 3, 9, 1]
rows = [(1, 30), (2, 10), (3, 20)]
ws = ["bbb", "a", "cc"]
n = 10

# unary / arithmetic / comparison — no call anywhere
print(sorted(xs, key=lambda v: -v))
print(list(map(lambda v: v * 2, xs)))
print(list(map(lambda v: v + n, xs)))
print(list(filter(lambda v: v > 3, xs)))

# SUBSCRIPT body: the sort-key idiom, and the single most common lambda in
# Python. A subscript opens a bracket, so it never counted as a call.
print(sorted(rows, key=lambda r: r[1]))
print(list(map(lambda r: r[0], rows)))

# ternary, boolean ops, `in`
print(list(map(lambda v: v if v > 3 else 0, xs)))
print(list(map(lambda v: v > 3 and v < 9, xs)))
print(list(map(lambda s: s in ws, ws)))

# a one-token body — under the old 3-token floor this could not lift either
ident = lambda v: v
print(ident(7))

# captured enclosing value, still call-free
mul = lambda v: v * n
print(mul(4))

# defaulted-parameter capture (Python's pin-a-value idiom), call-free body
pin = lambda v=n: v + 1
print(pin())

# stored in a variable, called repeatedly — the shape sorted()/map() use
sq = lambda v: v * v
print(sq(7), sq(3))

# min/max with a call-free key
print(min(xs, key=lambda v: -v), max(xs, key=lambda v: -v))

# CONTROLS — shapes that were ALREADY lifted must not change
print(list(map(lambda s: s.upper(), ws)))
print((lambda a: a + 1)(41))
add = lambda a: lambda b: a + b
print(add(3)(4))
